## Request

Build the smallest complete attention and recent-change slice on the existing hosted dashboard.
Derive attention only from controlled accepted fields and server-owned reason mappings. Preserve
instance freshness, stable identity, first/current timestamps, deterministic clearing, and safe
local investigation guidance. Normalize existing lifecycle and material events for recent review,
and mark entries since the last browser visit without creating server-side acknowledgement state.

## Contract Decisions

- Active attention reasons are controlled server-side: blocked work, unreconciled outcomes,
  retained App Server failure groups, and stale/offline reporting instances.
- Project-level counts never hide a stale or failing instance behind a fresh peer.
- The visit marker is browser-local presentation state. It does not clear, resolve, mutate, or
  suppress an active attention condition.
- Lifecycle and material events remain the change-history authority; the view normalizes them but
  does not copy or fabricate events.
- Suggested routes are fixed server-owned text: `ts: status`, `ts: doctor`,
  `ts: dashboard status`, or the relevant read-only dashboard detail.
- Existing retention and semantic SSE invalidation are reused.

